  "scope": "The complete theorem of Federer 3.2.15, p. 252: fibres of a globally Lipschitz Euclidean map R^m to R^n with m>n are countably (H^(m-n),m-n) rectifiable almost everywhere. Proved bounded-image decomposition, actual full-rank inverse-slice parametrizations for every target point, critical and nondifferentiable null-fibre reductions, and exact almost-containment. Target dimension zero is included; no finite fibre-mass, source measurability or extra rank premise.",
